Package: rhodep-modem-support
Version: 4
Architecture: arm64
Depends: qcom-support-common
Maintainer: rhodep port
Description: Modem/ADSP/CDSP + WiFi (WCN3990) support for Motorola rhodep
 Mounts modem_a firmware partition, symlinks .mbn->.mdt for the remoteprocs
 and the protection-domain .jsn files into the firmware directory pd-mapper
 looks in, sets rmtfs flags, brings up remoteprocs, and loads ath10k_snoc late
 (after the WLAN protection domain / QMI wlfw appears). Enables WiFi and BT.
 .
 The .jsn symlinks are what let pd-mapper publish the SERVREG locator, without
 which no protection domain starts: WLAN's wlan_pd and the sensor core's
 sensor_pd both depend on it.
 .
 Also delays ModemManager until the modem has registered its QMI services, and
 puts an apt hold on the packages this port depends on being exactly as
 validated (see the postinst).
